rld relevance. Our graduates are consistently sought after by local districts, and our long-standing reputation for excellence reflects the quality of our faculty and curriculum. As the only Christian university in the region, FPU offers a uniquely values-driven environment—and we are actively looking for experienced school and district administrators who are passionate about developing future educational leaders. To learn more about the program and course offerings, please visit our website at fresno.edu . Essential Functions Teach courses as described and assigned Discuss class progress with the program coordinator, including teaching performance through observation Collaborate with other faculty as needed Demonstrate a commitment to serving and inspiring students in an academic context that integrates your Christian faith and learning. Embrace the mission, vision , and values of Fresno Pacific University, affirm the FPU Faith Expectations , and support the ideals and practices articulated in \" The Fresno Pacific Idea ” Other job duties as assigned Qualifications Required: M.A. or Ph.D. in related field of study Experience as a K-12 public school or district administrator Hold a Clear Administrative Services credential Ability to work with students, staff, and faculty in a collegial environment Commitment to the Christian faith and the University’s mission of Christ-centered teaching and learning and involvement in a local church. Preferred: Ed.D. or Ph.D. in related discipline Environmental Conditions: Indoors in a normal office environment with little exposure to excessive noise, dust, fumes, vibrations, and temperature changes at least eighty percent (80%) of the time. Frequent computer use at a workstation, up to eight hours per day. Frequently work at a fast pace with unscheduled interruptions. Drive personal or University vehicles to appointments. Public contact position requiring professional apparel, personal hygiene, and grooming. Physical Demands: This 